  "task_version": 2,
  "query": "I'm done replacing headphones every two years. Headbands crack, earpads flake, batteries give up. This time I want one pair of over-ears I can still be wearing in 2036, even if that means paying more up front or going wired. What actually kills headphones over the years, and does going wireless doom me from the start because of the battery? Do replaceable pads and cables genuinely matter or is that a spec-sheet gimmick? I want to hear what long-term owners say survived a decade of daily use, and then the one pair you'd bet on.",
